Open • FLYBYME (Tim) opened about 12 minutes ago • 1 comment
Labels: bug


   describeExposure  (mesh-serve  src/api/schema/descriptor.ts ) builds a     
  complete                                                                    
  machine-readable description of every exposed call —  key ,  domain ,       
  action                                                                      
  ,                                                                           
   description ,  method ,  path ,  gate ,  input ,  output ,  destructive ,  
   stream ,  errors . It is consumed at build time to emit the typed client   
  and                                                                         
  then discarded.                                                             
                                                                              
  The browser gets method and path and nothing else, because  ApiCall.types   
  is a                                                                        
  phantom by design ( mesh-web/src/net/api.ts:33  — "Never assigned. Present  
  only                                                                        
  so the compiler carries the shapes.").                                      
                                                                              
  Two consequences, both live today:                                          
                                                                              
  1. The gate is a comment.  mesh-core/src/generated/api.ts  documents each   
  call as  auth: public . The console site's own row declares  auth: 'user'   
  for                                                                         
  all eighteen of its contracts except  identity.ticket_issue , and the server
  answers:                                                                    
                                                                              
    $ curl 'http://127.0.0.1:5005/api/parts?limit=2' -H 'Host: console.       
  localhost'                                                                  
    {"error":"UNAUTHENTICATED","message":"part.find requires a valid ticket."}
                                                                              
  So the one artifact a developer would read to find out whether a call needs 
  auth                                                                        
  says the opposite of the truth, and nothing can check it because the gate   
  never                                                                       
  becomes runtime data.                                                       
                                                                              
  2. No client can adapt to it. An Application cannot ask "does this call need
  a session?", so it cannot hold a request that is certain to 401, and cannot 
  know                                                                        
  to retry when a session appears.                                            
                                                                              
  See  mesh-web/spec/schema-driven-ui.md  §1 and §3.1, and roadmap B13.       


FLYBYME (Owner) • 3m • Newest comment

  ### Plan for #39: Serve the exposure descriptor and emit runtime gate data  
                                                                              
  #### Found                                                                  
                                                                              
  • Live node curl ( curl -i 'http://127.0.0.1:5005/api/parts?limit=2' -H     
  'Host: console.localhost' ) answers  401 UNAUTHENTICATED  ( part.find       
  requires a valid ticket. ).                                                 
  •  mesh-core/src/generated/api.ts  recorded  auth: public  only in JSDoc    
  comments;  src/api/methods/client.ts:110  emits  call(method, path)         
  dropping the gate from runtime data entirely.                               
  •  src/api/api.service.ts  routes  /events  via  EVENTS_PATH , but has no   
  route or handler for  GET /api/_describe .                                  
  •  describeExposure  in  src/api/schema/descriptor.ts  enforces deny-by-    
  default for internal contracts when  allowInternal  is falsy.               
                                                                              
  #### Changes                                                                
                                                                              
  1.  src/api/api.service.ts :                                                
    • Add  export const DESCRIBE_PATH = '/_describe' .                        
    • Route  inner === DESCRIBE_PATH  in  handle()  to  this.describe(req, res,
    site, release, origin) .                                                  
    • Gate on  _describe : Choose  public . The route map allows              
    unauthenticated clients (e.g., schema-driven UI / models before sign-in,  
    CI tools) to discover required auth levels in advance and display login   
    forms rather than triggering 401s (refs #40). Internal contracts are      
    withheld by  describeExposure 's deny-by-default.                         
    • Cache headers: Send  etag: descriptor.exposure  and  cache-control: no- 
    cache ; return  304  when  if-none-match  matches.                        
    • Shape hash: Response carries  x-exposure-shape: descriptor.shapeHash    
    and deliberately omits  x-exposure .                                      
    • Derive and cache  ExposureDescriptor  per site/release ( allowInternal: 
    false ).                                                                  
  2.  src/api/methods/client.ts :                                             
    • Update  entry()  in  emitClient()  to emit the structural gate literal  
    as a runtime argument on  call(method, path, gate) .                      
  3. Tests:                                                                   
    • In  test/integration/api.test.ts : verify  GET /api/_describe  returns  
    exposed calls and no internal contracts, carries  x-exposure-shape  and   
    not  x-exposure , supports  ETag  /  304 , and is accessible with public  
    gate.                                                                     
    • In  test/api/exposure.test.ts : verify generated client carries the gate
    as a readable runtime value matching declared site gates.                 
                                                                              
                                                                              
  #### Not Touching                                                           
                                                                              
  • No UI/forms/components (mesh-web).                                        
  • No gate changes on existing sites.                                        
  • Not touching  catalog.publish .                                           
  • Not modifying or regenerating  mesh-core  (different repo).               
                                                                              
